>Make sharp software videos</h1>
<p>A focused Fireship-inspired production course for Aadil.</p>
<p><a id=3D"preface"></a></p>
<h2>Start here</h2>
<p>Learn a small set of skills in order: choose the explanation, write it, =
record the voice, capture evidence, assemble the pictures, then polish. Sta=
rt with a 90=E2=80=93150-second developer explainer. Keep your own perspect=
ive and humour.</p>
<p>This focused course uses your eight-to-ten-hour weekly schedule and scre=
en-first filming preference. Work through one lesson each week. The reusabl=
e playbook comes afterward, when the basic operations feel familiar. Six we=
eks establishes a practice system; it does not guarantee parity with a prof=
essional creator.</p>
<p>Historical facts about Jeff's process are dated and separated from our o=
riginal recipes. The equipment recommendations are for your needs. His curr=
ent exact gear, presets and private workflow remain unverified. The resourc=
e links teach the relevant operation; there is no requirement to complete a=
n entire certification before making a video.</p>
