<p><a id=3D"chapter-01"></a></p>
<h2>01 =E2=80=94 Study the decisions, then make a small setup</h2>
<p><strong>Your result this week:</strong> a short reference analysis, one =
editor ready to use, and a clean twenty-second recording. Use 8.5 hours tot=
al. You already know programming; you do not need editing experience.</p>
<p><a id=3D"chapter-01-section-1"></a></p>
<h3>What we actually know about the reference</h3>
<p>Jeff's <a href=3D"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DN6-Q2dgodLs">2020 pr=
oduction walkthrough</a> documents Premiere, After Effects, Figma and a voi=
ceover-first process. Around 5:55 he says that not every video begins with =
a written script; around 6:07 he describes short recorded phrases. At 7:33 =
he explains revealing prepared code with Undo; at 7:53 he discusses frame h=
olds. These are dated first-person statements, not a verified 2026 equipmen=
t list.</p>
<p>That changes the way you should learn. The polished result does not requ=
ire flawless live coding. You can prepare a working example, record a clear=
 explanation, then construct the visual sequence that makes the explanation=
 easy to follow. For a beginner, a written script is helpful even though hi=
s historical method could be more improvised. Preparation should suit your =
current skill.</p>
<p>The selected frames of <a href=3D"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3Dx7X9=
w_GIm1s">Python in 100 Seconds</a> show a large text card around 0:28, an o=
versized numeral over an image around 0:57, and a visual joke beside code a=
round 1:25. That establishes some visual ingredients. It does not establish=
 an average cut rate, exact keyframe curves or a retention benefit. The fol=
lowing exercises are your own adaptations.</p>
<p><a id=3D"chapter-01-section-2"></a></p>
<h3>Choose the format you are learning</h3>
<p>Fireship is not one uniform template. A compact concept overview, a news=
 commentary and a project tutorial have different jobs. Start with the comp=
act concept overview. It has the smallest research and filming surface, let=
s you repeat editing practice, and fits your preference for screen recordin=
gs and occasional camera segments.</p>
<p>Your first topic is =E2=80=9CA valid JSON answer can still be wrong.=E2=
=80=9D It fits your practical AI/software interests and has a tiny demonstr=
able contradiction. You do not need an entire AI application. The supplied =
synthetic example parses successfully and fails a simple arithmetic check. =
That is enough to teach the distinction without claiming to solve all AI re=
liability problems.</p>
<p>For your reference map, watch thirty seconds of a chosen reference three=
 ways. First listen for the order of ideas. Second watch muted and name the=
 job of each visual: orient, explain, prove, emphasize or joke. Third watch=
 normally and note when an image appears relative to the spoken idea. Use y=
our own words; do not transcribe or collect an entire asset library from an=
other creator.</p>
<p>Your notes might say: =E2=80=9CDefinition arrives before history; the ke=
y term becomes large text; code appears only when syntax matters.=E2=80=9D =
These are useful observations. =E2=80=9CThe secret is a cut every 1.7 secon=
ds=E2=80=9D is an unsupported rule unless you actually measured that sample=
, and still would not describe the whole channel. Count visual changes sepa=
rately from full cuts: a label appearing over code is a new visual beat wit=
hout a new shot.</p>
<p><a id=3D"chapter-01-section-3"></a></p>
<h3>Make a deliberate editor choice</h3>
<p>Use <a href=3D"https://www.blackmagicdesign.com/products/davinciresolve"=
>DaVinci Resolve free</a> for the main learning path. It lets you practice =
timeline editing, audio, text and basic motion without committing to a subs=
cription. Its current product page identifies Resolve 21; some official tra=
ining books remain labeled 20. Follow concepts and look up changed controls=
 in the installed version.</p>
<p>If you already have Premiere, use it. The important equivalents are time=
line cutting, ripple deletion, markers, transform keyframes, a still/frame =
hold, text layers and audio gain. After Effects becomes useful for more ela=
borate motion later; it is not required to make your first clean explainer.=
 Do not buy plugins before you can make a convincing basic title and code h=
ighlight yourself.</p>
<p>Open the <a href=3D"https://www.blackmagicdesign.com/products/davincires=
olve/training">official training index</a>. This week use Introduction to E=
diting Part 1 and only the sections needed to import, assemble, trim and ex=
port a short clip. It is an inspected learning index, not a claim that ever=
y training video was watched during this research. Adobe users can use <a h=
ref=3D"https://www.adobe.com/learn/premiere-pro">Get to know Premiere</a> i=
nstead. One completed test matters more than collecting courses.</p>
<p><a id=3D"chapter-01-section-4"></a></p>
<h3>Make the first recording before shopping</h3>
<p>Record twenty seconds explaining the JSON distinction with your current =
microphone. Use a quiet room with soft furnishings, turn off distracting fa=
ns where practical, and position the microphone consistently. Replay the fi=
le. Is the speech clear? Is there an audible room echo? Are strong consonan=
ts causing thumps? Is the level clipping? Each problem has a different reme=
dy.</p>
<p>Echo calls for a better room or closer sensible placement before heavier=
 processing. Plosive thumps call for a slight off-axis angle and a pop filt=
er. Clipping calls for lower input gain and a new take. A pricey microphone=
 does not fix a take already recorded with distorted peaks. The <a href=3D"=
file:///C:/Users/amallick.ENGINEERS/OneDrive%20-%20Unison%20Software,%20Inc=
/Documents/ChatGPT/My%20career%20growth%20and%20side%20hustle%20income/fire=
ship-production-playbook/course.html#equipment">equipment decision</a> give=
s one straightforward purchase path if your existing recording is the limit=
ing factor.</p>
<p>Import that recording into the editor, split around a mistaken phrase, r=
emove it, and export the result. Listen outside the editor. This confirms t=
he whole chain. Save the working project as a reusable template with separa=
te dialogue, music and sound-effect tracks, and bins named Voice, Screens, =
Graphics and Exports. You can change the names; the purpose is separating m=
aterial you need to find quickly.</p>
